WEBVTT


00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:27.716 --> 00:02:31.820
It's two plus two
equals six.


00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.691
I will never tell you.


00:02:36.721 --> 00:02:37.893
But you will.


00:02:38.031 --> 00:02:43.228
OPERATION DUNKIRK


00:02:44.191 --> 00:02:47.691
Subrip: Pix
<font color=#ff0000>subs4free.info</font>


00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:21.173
<i>The enemy attacked us
on all sides</i>


00:03:21.203 --> 00:03:23.775
<i>with great strength
and fierceness.</i>


00:03:23.805 --> 00:03:26.745
<i>Pressing in upon
the narrow exit,</i>


00:03:26.775 --> 00:03:28.947
<i>both from the east
and from the west,</i>


00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:32.183
<i>the enemy began
to fire with cannon</i>


00:03:32.213 --> 00:03:34.816
<i>upon the beaches by
which alone the shipping</i>


00:03:34.846 --> 00:03:37.588
<i>could approach or depart.</i>


00:03:37.618 --> 00:03:40.672
<i>Meanwhile, the Royal Navy
with the willing help</i>


00:03:40.702 --> 00:03:43.757
<i>of countless Merchant
Seamen strained</i>


00:03:43.758 --> 00:03:48.796
<i>every nerve to embark
the British and Allied troops.</i>


00:03:48.826 --> 00:03:52.037
<i>Two-hundred and twenty light
warships</i>


00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:56.275
<i>and 650 other vessels
were engaged.</i>


00:03:56.305 --> 00:03:58.840
<i>They had to operate
upon a difficult coast</i>


00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:02.246
<i>often in adverse weather</i>


00:04:02.276 --> 00:04:06.214
<i>under an almost
ceaseless hail of bombs</i>


00:04:06.215 --> 00:04:10.485
<i>and an increasing concentration
of artillery fire.</i>


00:04:10.515 --> 00:04:12.824
<i>Nor were the seas,
as I have said,</i>


00:04:12.854 --> 00:04:15.926
<i>themselves free
from mines and torpedoes.</i>


00:04:15.956 --> 00:04:18.492
<i>It was in conditions
such as these that our men</i>


00:04:18.522 --> 00:04:21.912
<i>carried on with
little or no rest.</i>


00:04:21.942 --> 00:04:25.303
<i>For days and nights on end,</i>


00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:29.340
<i>making trip after trip
across the dangerous waters,</i>


00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.608
<i>bringing with them always
men whom they had rescued.</i>


00:04:56.497 --> 00:04:58.550
Attention!


00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.604
At ease.


00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:03.474
Lt. Calloway?


00:05:03.504 --> 00:05:06.192
This must be your lucky day.


00:05:06.222 --> 00:05:08.881
You're not being evacuated.


00:05:08.911 --> 00:05:11.831
You might actually
live another day.


00:05:11.861 --> 00:05:14.675
It's a ruddy
bloodbath out there!


00:05:14.705 --> 00:05:17.489
Gentlemen, battles
will be won


00:05:17.519 --> 00:05:20.120
by the side that
first spots enemy airplanes,


00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:22.159
ships or submarines.


00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:24.526
And British scientists have
been working feverishly


00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:27.561
to develop radar
technology that will see


00:05:27.591 --> 00:05:30.597
for hundreds of miles,
even at night.


00:05:30.598 --> 00:05:34.304
But they haven't been
able to crack it.


00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.837
Just recently, we got
intelligence from the Americans.


00:05:36.838 --> 00:05:38.306
The Americans?


00:05:38.336 --> 00:05:39.643
Yes.


00:05:39.673 --> 00:05:42.476
Seems a German scientist
has developed this technology


00:05:42.506 --> 00:05:45.279
but doesn't want
to share it with Hitler.


00:05:45.309 --> 00:05:47.184
I know.


00:05:47.214 --> 00:05:49.253
Whatever his reasons,
he wants to share it with us.


00:05:49.283 --> 00:05:53.788
Therefore, I need you and your
men to go retrieve the package.


00:05:53.818 --> 00:05:55.856
The package being?


00:05:55.857 --> 00:05:57.794
The German scientist.


00:05:57.824 --> 00:05:59.729
Do we know where this
package is, sir?


00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.898
Yes. We're being told
the French Resistance has


00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:05.332
the German scientist in a
safe house not far from here.


00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:10.706
He's being held here
in an old factory


00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.410
right off of L'Autoroute A25.


00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.179
That's 51 degrees north,
37 east.


00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:19.079
You're to go there,
rendezvous with the French,


00:06:19.109 --> 00:06:21.915
retrieve the package,
and get out.


00:06:21.945 --> 00:06:23.354
Any questions?


00:06:23.384 --> 00:06:25.687
Much enemy activity
in the area, sir?


00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:28.039
From our reports,
little to none.


00:06:28.069 --> 00:06:30.391
The French are
expecting you.


00:06:30.421 --> 00:06:32.296
Once you've made contact,


00:06:32.326 --> 00:06:34.528
they will ask you for
a piece of paper.


00:06:34.558 --> 00:06:36.730
Give them this.


00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.236
Sir.


00:06:38.266 --> 00:06:39.970
Any more questions?


00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.204
So we're not going to be
evacuated, then. Is that it?


00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:45.873
You have your orders.


00:06:45.874 --> 00:06:49.210
Pull your balls out of your
throat and be a soldier!


00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.111
- Yes, sir!
- Get your kit together


00:06:51.112 --> 00:06:53.382
and get ready to move out.
Do you understand me?


00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:54.483
Yes, sir!


00:06:56.384 --> 00:07:00.588
This mission could
not only save lives,


00:07:00.618 --> 00:07:02.057
but win the war.


00:07:03.925 --> 00:07:06.028
Carry on.


00:07:17.137 --> 00:07:19.106
You heard the colonel.


00:07:19.107 --> 00:07:21.242
Little to no enemy activity.


00:07:21.272 --> 00:07:22.313
We get in, we get out.


00:07:22.343 --> 00:07:24.482
We don't miss the evacuation.


00:07:24.512 --> 00:07:27.281
Just one last roll
of the dice, lads.


00:07:32.519 --> 00:07:33.621
Let's go.


00:08:29.943 --> 00:08:32.764
Should be just over
this field.


00:08:32.794 --> 00:08:35.616
Better proceed
with caution.


00:09:20.294 --> 00:09:22.197
Into the bushes!


00:10:00.467 --> 00:10:03.471
You must love your
family very much, no?


00:10:05.472 --> 00:10:07.475
Do you realize that
we know where they are?


00:10:09.277 --> 00:10:13.948
My soldiers are on their way
right now to pick them up.


00:10:13.978 --> 00:10:17.852
<i>Mein familia has
nothing to do with this!</i>


00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:33.634
No!


00:10:40.251 --> 00:10:43.588
Tell me!


00:11:01.714 --> 00:11:05.087
Okay.
Okay.


00:11:05.117 --> 00:11:08.289
I give it
to a young woman,


00:11:08.319 --> 00:11:13.825
French Resistance
on her way to BAF now.


00:11:22.166 --> 00:11:24.436
Angelique!


00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.243
Show me where she is.


00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:55.800
They will see you
soon enough.


00:12:31.596 --> 00:12:33.433
Everything all right, Thomas?


00:12:33.463 --> 00:12:36.200
It's my son's birthday
in two weeks.


00:12:36.201 --> 00:12:39.573
I just really
wanted to see him.


00:12:39.603 --> 00:12:43.541
I haven't seen him
yet since he was born.


00:12:46.276 --> 00:12:47.711
Don't worry about it,
Thomas.


00:12:47.712 --> 00:12:50.867
You'll see him on his
next birthday, yeah?


00:12:50.897 --> 00:12:53.510
You can tell him what
a hero his father is.


00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.154
Never actually been
with a woman myself.


00:12:56.184 --> 00:12:58.088
You never been with a woman?


00:12:58.118 --> 00:13:00.157
Not intimately, no.


00:13:00.158 --> 00:13:02.828
So you've not had a shag?


00:13:02.858 --> 00:13:05.529
Such a romantic, Walker.


00:13:10.034 --> 00:13:11.273
Let's just find this kraut,


00:13:11.303 --> 00:13:13.505
and get the hell
out of France, yeah?


00:13:13.535 --> 00:13:15.275
What do you say?


00:13:15.305 --> 00:13:18.210
I hate this country.
It stinks.


00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:21.115
Lieutenant, all due respect,


00:13:21.145 --> 00:13:23.914
how do we know we can
trust this scientist?


00:13:23.944 --> 00:13:26.687
He is German, after all.


00:13:26.717 --> 00:13:30.053
Because cleverer men
than us have told us so.


00:13:30.083 --> 00:13:32.122
Well, they better be right.


00:13:34.058 --> 00:13:35.994
This must be it, lads.


00:13:39.329 --> 00:13:40.431
Stay sharp.


00:14:04.789 --> 00:14:06.609
Drop your weapons!


00:14:06.639 --> 00:14:10.894
Lower your guns!


00:14:10.895 --> 00:14:12.831
I said drop your guns!


00:14:12.861 --> 00:14:14.798
Turn!


00:14:14.799 --> 00:14:16.134
Turn slowly to me!


00:14:20.704 --> 00:14:21.742
Turn slowly!


00:14:21.772 --> 00:14:23.474
What is your business here?


00:14:25.343 --> 00:14:28.213
We're with the British
Expeditionary Force.


00:14:28.243 --> 00:14:30.531
We've come
to collect a package.


00:14:30.561 --> 00:14:32.850
You should have
a package for me.


00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.352
Yes. Yes, I do.


00:14:50.568 --> 00:14:51.606
Read it.


00:14:51.636 --> 00:14:53.805
Read it to me!


00:14:58.309 --> 00:15:00.729
"The children long
to play in the fields


00:15:00.759 --> 00:15:03.150
but had to settle
instead for the sand


00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:06.350
which was accompanied
by an enormous roar."


00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.586
All right, where is he?


00:15:09.587 --> 00:15:11.924
How many are with you?


00:15:11.954 --> 00:15:14.292
Just the five of us.


00:15:17.027 --> 00:15:18.829
All right, where is he?


00:15:18.859 --> 00:15:21.499
She is inside.


00:15:23.834 --> 00:15:26.469
Wait. She?


00:15:27.705 --> 00:15:29.173
You did not know.


00:15:29.174 --> 00:15:31.275
No. I thought we were
collecting the chap


00:15:31.305 --> 00:15:34.127
with the algorithm
for radar.


00:15:34.157 --> 00:15:36.938
You were until
he was captured


00:15:36.968 --> 00:15:39.749
by Nazi but moments
before this.


00:15:39.779 --> 00:15:40.951
He gave the algorithm.


00:15:40.981 --> 00:15:42.285
To Angelique.


00:15:42.286 --> 00:15:43.954
Angelique?


00:15:45.256 --> 00:15:48.927
<i>- Oui.
- All right, let's go.</i>


00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:17.991
Angelique?


00:16:18.021 --> 00:16:19.160
<i>C'est moi, Pierre.</i>


00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:22.727
Don't shoot, don't shoot.


00:16:22.757 --> 00:16:25.500
This is her.


00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:26.700
You have the algorithm?


00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:29.833
<i>- Oui.
- May I see it?</i>


00:16:29.834 --> 00:16:33.404
I have not written it down.
So you must keep me alive.


00:16:33.434 --> 00:16:35.038
Very sensible.


00:16:35.039 --> 00:16:36.741
Then we should leave.


00:16:36.771 --> 00:16:37.979
What's the plan?


00:16:38.009 --> 00:16:40.612
We must get her
to this location.


00:16:40.642 --> 00:16:42.346
They will further assist her.


00:16:42.347 --> 00:16:46.050
They have arranged a plane
to take her to Great Britain.


00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:50.788
But we must wait
for the Americans.


00:16:50.818 --> 00:16:52.726
They're already late.


00:16:52.756 --> 00:16:54.358
So I'm assuming the worst.


00:16:54.388 --> 00:16:55.560
We need to move.


00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:59.330
Shit! We've got company!


00:17:02.032 --> 00:17:04.636
So much for little
to no enemy activity.


00:17:04.666 --> 00:17:05.807
Take cover.


00:17:05.837 --> 00:17:07.623
I'll see if I
can delay them.


00:17:07.653 --> 00:17:09.409
All right,
let's dig in, lads.


00:17:09.439 --> 00:17:12.108
We were given a mission
and I plan on completing it.


00:17:12.138 --> 00:17:14.044
Harris, get me the colonel
on the wireless.


00:17:14.074 --> 00:17:15.282
Yes, sir.


00:17:15.312 --> 00:17:19.251
F13C here.
Come in, Dunkirk.


00:17:19.281 --> 00:17:23.221
F13C.
This is Colonel Plummer.


00:17:23.251 --> 00:17:25.056
Sir, I have the colonel.


00:17:28.393 --> 00:17:30.995
We're at the destination, sir.
But the package isn't here.


00:17:31.025 --> 00:17:32.433
<i>There is a French girl
with the Resistance.</i>


00:17:32.463 --> 00:17:34.531
<i>Said she was given
the algorithm by the scientist</i>


00:17:34.561 --> 00:17:36.466
<i>before he was captured
by the Nazis.</i>


00:17:36.496 --> 00:17:38.334
<i>Has she showed it to you?</i>


00:17:38.335 --> 00:17:40.805
Says she has it
memorized, sir.


00:17:40.835 --> 00:17:42.242
Blood hell!


00:17:42.272 --> 00:17:43.675
That changes things.


00:17:43.705 --> 00:17:45.078
One more thing, sir.


00:17:45.108 --> 00:17:46.577
We also appear
to have company.


00:17:46.607 --> 00:17:47.815
How many?


00:17:47.845 --> 00:17:49.316
Difficult to say.


00:17:49.346 --> 00:17:51.284
Looks like a transport
heading our way.


00:17:51.314 --> 00:17:53.884
Get your asses out of there
before they arrive!


00:17:53.885 --> 00:17:55.088
<i>Those are your orders!</i>


00:17:55.118 --> 00:17:57.554
Understood, sir.
F13C out.


00:18:00.223 --> 00:18:01.927
You don't trust me?


00:18:01.957 --> 00:18:03.661
They've arrived!


00:18:14.105 --> 00:18:18.076
It's the Germans.
On the left and right.


00:18:30.053 --> 00:18:32.589
We know you are in there!


00:18:32.619 --> 00:18:33.724
Come out!


00:19:33.416 --> 00:19:35.822
She's in there right now.


00:19:35.852 --> 00:19:40.657
Yes, sir, but she has been
joined by five BAF soldiers.


00:19:47.698 --> 00:19:49.266
And they are
in there right now?


00:19:49.296 --> 00:19:50.870
Are you sure?


00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:54.737
Yes, sir. They just arrived
maybe four or five minutes ago.


00:19:54.767 --> 00:19:56.340
They are well-armed.


00:20:05.983 --> 00:20:07.187
And the Americans?


00:20:07.217 --> 00:20:10.657
No, sir.
I have not seen them.


00:20:10.687 --> 00:20:13.323
And she has
the algorithm for sure?


00:20:14.858 --> 00:20:16.360
<i>Oui.</i>


00:20:18.329 --> 00:20:20.298
What is he doing?


00:20:43.119 --> 00:20:44.990
Excellent work.


00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.691
Merci, sir.


00:20:46.721 --> 00:20:48.392
May I leave?


00:20:52.797 --> 00:20:54.966
You have five seconds
to run for your life.


00:20:54.996 --> 00:20:58.505
No! No, sir!


00:20:58.535 --> 00:21:01.705
Sir, no!
Please! No, no!


00:21:17.821 --> 00:21:20.257
Damn it!


00:21:21.358 --> 00:21:22.663
The traitor sold us out.


00:21:22.693 --> 00:21:24.829
Let's concentrate
on the task in hand.


00:21:24.859 --> 00:21:26.363
I count ten men.


00:21:26.393 --> 00:21:28.081
Same here, sir.


00:21:28.111 --> 00:21:29.770
Can we trust you?


00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:32.606
I risked my life
to fight the Germans!


00:21:32.636 --> 00:21:35.606
I watched as my mother
and father begged for their life


00:21:35.636 --> 00:21:38.542
and the life
of my brother and sister!


00:21:38.572 --> 00:21:41.449
They were only eight
and nine years old!


00:21:41.479 --> 00:21:43.547
They'll do the same thing
to her if we leave her.


00:21:43.577 --> 00:21:45.482
No one said anything
about leaving her.


00:21:45.512 --> 00:21:47.221
We heard the colonel, sir.


00:21:47.251 --> 00:21:49.220
You swear you have
the algorithm?


00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:50.788
It's all I have!


00:21:54.591 --> 00:21:57.130
We know you are in there!


00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:00.697
To the British
soldiers inside:


00:22:00.727 --> 00:22:02.065
Send us the girl


00:22:02.066 --> 00:22:03.568
and you will all go free.


00:22:13.211 --> 00:22:16.381
Otherwise, you will
experience the same fate


00:22:16.411 --> 00:22:19.184
as your French friend here.


00:22:24.387 --> 00:22:27.759
She will never give
the algorithm to the Allies.


00:22:27.789 --> 00:22:29.230
Ever!


00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:31.896
You send her out,
you will all go free!


00:22:37.769 --> 00:22:41.839
You have two minutes
to send her out.


00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:52.052
No.


00:22:52.082 --> 00:22:53.320
No, no, please!


00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:55.819
Please! Please!
I am telling the truth!


00:22:55.849 --> 00:22:56.857
Please!


00:22:56.887 --> 00:23:00.157
Please, you must
believe me! Please!


00:23:00.187 --> 00:23:01.658
Gentlemen?


00:23:09.366 --> 00:23:11.169
Speak freely, lads.
You heard the colonel.


00:23:11.199 --> 00:23:12.936
You know the mission.


00:23:24.415 --> 00:23:26.087
Well, I want to go home.


00:23:26.117 --> 00:23:28.554
We don't even know
if she has the algorithm.


00:23:28.584 --> 00:23:31.021
And how do we know
this algorithm can even do


00:23:31.051 --> 00:23:32.656
what people say
it can?


00:23:35.525 --> 00:23:37.461
Give her to them.


00:23:37.462 --> 00:23:38.829
How can we really trust her?


00:23:44.935 --> 00:23:48.539
I couldn't live with myself
if we turned her in, sir.


00:23:48.569 --> 00:23:51.677
Let's complete the mission.


00:23:51.707 --> 00:23:53.577
I've always thought it's
a soldier's duty


00:23:53.578 --> 00:23:55.846
to protect those who
can't protect themselves.


00:23:55.876 --> 00:23:58.381
Now there are ten of them
to our five,


00:23:58.411 --> 00:24:00.887
but we have
the elevated position.


00:24:00.917 --> 00:24:03.454
But, Lieutenant, they may
have reinforcements?


00:24:03.484 --> 00:24:05.091
Yes, that's quite possible,
Harris.


00:24:05.121 --> 00:24:08.124
But sometimes a man has
to take a stand on principle.


00:24:08.125 --> 00:24:10.728
No matter the consequences.


00:24:12.462 --> 00:24:13.901
I'm with you, sir.


00:24:13.931 --> 00:24:16.668
You say and I'll fill them
so full of lead,


00:24:16.698 --> 00:24:18.569
it'll be coming
out their eyes.


00:24:29.347 --> 00:24:31.351
Thank you, gentlemen.


00:24:31.381 --> 00:24:33.884
You will not regret this!
Thank you.


00:24:37.487 --> 00:24:39.491
All right,
Fritz, we've talked.


00:24:39.521 --> 00:24:41.495
We're not
bringing her out,


00:24:41.525 --> 00:24:43.827
so you're gonna have
to come in and get her!


00:24:43.828 --> 00:24:45.629
Fire!


00:24:56.106 --> 00:24:58.041
Pull out!


00:24:59.243 --> 00:25:00.778
Pull out!


00:25:04.381 --> 00:25:05.600
Patch him up, man.


00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:06.819
Am I gonna die?


00:25:06.849 --> 00:25:09.437
- No.
- Am I gonna die?


00:25:09.467 --> 00:25:12.056
Am I gonna die?
Shit!


00:25:12.086 --> 00:25:13.725
Am I gonna die?


00:25:27.303 --> 00:25:29.072
Damn it!


00:25:35.846 --> 00:25:37.982
Sir!
I have some dynamite!


00:25:38.012 --> 00:25:39.020
Let me set a trap.


00:25:39.050 --> 00:25:41.519
I'll blow these bastards
to smithereens.


00:25:46.057 --> 00:25:48.126
Schreck!
I've got a schreck here!


00:25:48.156 --> 00:25:49.797
God, then
we're out-gunned!


00:25:49.827 --> 00:25:52.499
We gotta get outta here!
Any ideas?


00:25:52.529 --> 00:25:54.330
Let's go out the back way!
I know the forest!


00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:55.933
King, Walker, on Thomas!


00:25:55.963 --> 00:25:57.170
Go!


00:25:57.200 --> 00:25:58.636
Thomas, let's go!


00:27:03.134 --> 00:27:05.903
Let's keep moving.
Come on.


00:27:05.933 --> 00:27:07.070
Chins up.


00:27:10.840 --> 00:27:13.144
That's it.
This way.


00:27:18.515 --> 00:27:21.017
All right, mighty forty,
everyone down here.


00:27:50.214 --> 00:27:51.682
Come on!


00:27:53.916 --> 00:27:56.190
Stay with me. Come on.


00:27:56.220 --> 00:27:58.923
We're getting out of here.
We're getting out of here.


00:28:06.496 --> 00:28:08.031
Come on!
Hold it together, Thomas!


00:28:08.061 --> 00:28:09.403
We've got to move on, man!


00:28:09.433 --> 00:28:11.935
We're working
on this together.


00:28:11.965 --> 00:28:14.204
Pull it together, Thomas.


00:29:31.181 --> 00:29:33.869
So any chance of getting
medical support for Thomas?


00:29:33.899 --> 00:29:37.113
The wireless was destroyed.
There's no calling anyone.


00:29:37.143 --> 00:29:40.357
Are you sure we can trust
this location that he gave us?


00:29:40.387 --> 00:29:42.128
<i>Oui.</i>


00:29:42.158 --> 00:29:44.593
I mean, he was working for the
Germans, it may be compromised.


00:29:44.623 --> 00:29:46.098
I don't think so.


00:29:46.128 --> 00:29:48.965
I don't think Pierre expected
us to escape. You know?


00:29:48.995 --> 00:29:51.204
Yes. You may have a point.


00:29:51.234 --> 00:29:53.435
Damn it, we need a radio!
We need to pause!


00:29:53.465 --> 00:29:54.587
I know a safe house.


00:29:54.617 --> 00:29:55.739
It might have a radio.


00:29:55.740 --> 00:29:57.907
- How far?
- Not far.


00:31:16.686 --> 00:31:20.627
- Shit!
- Sir!


00:31:20.657 --> 00:31:22.827
Sir, he's not doing so well.


00:31:27.364 --> 00:31:29.700
Sir, they're getting closer.
We'll never outrun them.


00:31:29.730 --> 00:31:31.234
Especially with him
in this state.


00:31:31.264 --> 00:31:32.769
Well, we can't
just leave him here!


00:31:32.799 --> 00:31:33.904
You are...


00:31:35.406 --> 00:31:39.046
You have to.


00:31:39.076 --> 00:31:41.278
I'm not going to make it.


00:31:41.308 --> 00:31:42.782
I know that.


00:31:42.812 --> 00:31:44.180
And you know that.


00:31:44.181 --> 00:31:46.801
This can't
be all for nothing.


00:31:46.831 --> 00:31:49.451
You said we could
be heroes.


00:31:49.452 --> 00:31:51.454
Now get her to safety!


00:31:52.356 --> 00:31:54.126
You're coming with us, Thomas.


00:31:54.156 --> 00:31:56.260
We're gonna get you home
to see your wife and son.


00:31:56.290 --> 00:32:00.731
You lads can do it,
but not with me.


00:32:00.761 --> 00:32:03.436
Not with me!


00:32:03.466 --> 00:32:05.953
You get home to England.


00:32:05.983 --> 00:32:08.471
You tell my son what I did.


00:32:08.472 --> 00:32:12.242
You tell him I was a hero.


00:32:12.272 --> 00:32:13.512
I shall.


00:32:13.542 --> 00:32:15.312
Reach into my pocket.


00:32:15.342 --> 00:32:17.530
- Here.
- This one?


00:32:17.560 --> 00:32:19.748
There. There's a letter.


00:32:19.749 --> 00:32:23.957
Please...


00:32:23.987 --> 00:32:26.489
Please give this
to my wife.


00:32:26.490 --> 00:32:28.825
You tell her...


00:32:32.229 --> 00:32:34.631
You tell her that
I loved her the minute


00:32:34.661 --> 00:32:37.267
I have laid eyes
on her.


00:32:37.268 --> 00:32:39.472
I promise.


00:32:39.502 --> 00:32:41.706
You keep that promise.


00:32:41.736 --> 00:32:43.940
I will.
I will, Thomas.


00:32:43.941 --> 00:32:46.446
All right. Now...


00:32:46.476 --> 00:32:50.480
Now sit me up
against that tree.


00:32:56.820 --> 00:32:59.290
And hand me my gun.


00:33:03.126 --> 00:33:05.295
You don't have
to do this, Thomas.


00:33:05.325 --> 00:33:06.896
Yes, I do.


00:33:08.531 --> 00:33:09.532
Now go!


00:33:11.268 --> 00:33:16.273
Monsieur, I'm so sorry.


00:33:16.303 --> 00:33:18.007
Go!


00:33:35.759 --> 00:33:38.165
Let's go.


00:33:38.195 --> 00:33:41.197
Come on, you bloody krauts!


00:36:08.077 --> 00:36:09.178
<i>Schiesse!</i>


00:36:23.861 --> 00:36:26.949
That'll slow 'em down.
But it won't stop 'em.


00:36:26.979 --> 00:36:30.067
If Angelique's secret is
as valuable as we think,


00:36:30.097 --> 00:36:32.471
- then nothing will stop them.
- It is.


00:36:32.501 --> 00:36:35.271
Well, at least Thomas has bought us
enough time to gain some distance.


00:36:35.272 --> 00:36:38.241
It's just north,
a few kilometers.


00:36:38.271 --> 00:36:39.911
Let's move on.


00:36:39.941 --> 00:36:42.278
Everyone stays alert.


00:36:56.059 --> 00:36:57.530
We need to rest.


00:36:57.560 --> 00:37:01.231
All right, let's stop
just for a moment.


00:37:03.899 --> 00:37:05.769
Be sure and conserve water.


00:37:10.138 --> 00:37:12.776
These blisters are
killing me.


00:37:19.983 --> 00:37:22.218
Sir, I've got
ammunition here!


00:37:22.248 --> 00:37:23.787
Stop! Freeze, King!


00:37:27.990 --> 00:37:30.759
Don't move.


00:37:30.760 --> 00:37:33.162
Shit!


00:37:35.964 --> 00:37:38.968
Is it booby trapped?


00:37:38.998 --> 00:37:40.239
Yes, sir.


00:37:40.269 --> 00:37:42.538
With a compression mine.


00:37:42.539 --> 00:37:45.542
Attached to a grenade.
A stick grenade, sir.


00:37:47.577 --> 00:37:49.279
Do you see where
it's connected?


00:37:49.309 --> 00:37:51.983
Yes, sir.


00:37:52.013 --> 00:37:54.186
About six feet to my left.


00:37:54.216 --> 00:37:56.619
Mr. King, I need you
to ever so slightly


00:37:56.620 --> 00:37:58.125
point to where
the grenade is.


00:37:58.155 --> 00:38:00.323
Don't move your head
or your hips at all.


00:38:00.353 --> 00:38:01.328
Do you understand?


00:38:01.358 --> 00:38:04.127
Just turn your
wrist and point.


00:38:29.318 --> 00:38:31.487
Do you see it?


00:38:31.488 --> 00:38:32.791
Yes.


00:38:32.821 --> 00:38:34.390
Yes, I see it.


00:38:37.059 --> 00:38:38.928
Could we cut the wire?


00:38:47.070 --> 00:38:49.924
I need you to stay
very, very still.


00:38:49.954 --> 00:38:52.808
We're going to get you
out of this.


00:38:52.809 --> 00:38:56.879
You have to absolutely
not budge in the slightest.


00:38:56.909 --> 00:38:58.515
Yes, sir.


00:39:09.359 --> 00:39:12.065
How bad is it?


00:39:12.095 --> 00:39:13.800
They've double-rigged it.


00:39:13.830 --> 00:39:16.533
There's a compression mine
under the butt of the rifle.


00:39:18.633 --> 00:39:20.870
As long as he keeps pressure
on that, it won't detonate.


00:39:20.900 --> 00:39:23.539
But the wire that's
attached to the grenade


00:39:23.569 --> 00:39:25.212
is already
under tension.


00:39:25.242 --> 00:39:28.312
We clip that,
the charge will blow.


00:39:31.147 --> 00:39:32.818
Shit.


00:39:32.848 --> 00:39:34.251
What do we do?


00:40:29.606 --> 00:40:31.941
I'm never going to be with
a woman now, am I, sir?


00:40:31.971 --> 00:40:33.179
Stay calm, Mr. King.


00:40:33.209 --> 00:40:35.396
We've got to do something.


00:40:35.426 --> 00:40:37.583
He's already struggling.


00:40:37.613 --> 00:40:39.883
Those Nazis can't
be too far back.


00:40:44.620 --> 00:40:46.525
What are you thinking, sir?


00:40:46.555 --> 00:40:48.691
The only thing I can do
is try to tackle him


00:40:48.721 --> 00:40:50.225
out of the blast area.


00:40:50.255 --> 00:40:51.663
That's insane!


00:40:51.693 --> 00:40:53.496
And keep your
voice down, man!


00:40:53.497 --> 00:40:55.201
We need to keep him
steady.


00:40:55.231 --> 00:40:57.098
Are you losing your mind,
Lieutenant.


00:40:57.128 --> 00:40:58.672
With all due respect, sir.


00:40:58.702 --> 00:41:00.639
Well, do you have
a better idea?


00:41:00.669 --> 00:41:02.256
If we had something
to dampen the blast,


00:41:02.286 --> 00:41:03.873
then that would be
a fine thing, but...


00:41:03.874 --> 00:41:07.644
Any branches we might find
would just add to the shrapnel.


00:41:10.412 --> 00:41:12.284
I think I can get him clear.


00:41:12.314 --> 00:41:17.253
Sergeant Walker, if you
would accompany me over here,


00:41:17.254 --> 00:41:19.422
we can deduce
the blast radius.


00:41:19.452 --> 00:41:22.059
What are best chances are.


00:41:26.062 --> 00:41:28.964
Appears to be a slightly
angled towards 11:00.


00:41:31.234 --> 00:41:33.572
This direction.


00:41:33.602 --> 00:41:36.041
A radius nearly five feet.


00:41:36.071 --> 00:41:40.042
Should have two to three
seconds before it goes.


00:41:51.053 --> 00:41:52.891
Shall we?


00:41:52.921 --> 00:41:54.875
Seek out cover,
Sergeant Walker.


00:41:54.905 --> 00:41:56.829
What are you going
to do, sir?


00:41:56.859 --> 00:41:59.995
Here's what we're
going to do, Mr. King.


00:42:03.733 --> 00:42:06.239
I am going to tackle you.


00:42:06.269 --> 00:42:08.574
You are going to stay
absolutely still


00:42:08.604 --> 00:42:10.573
until you feel
my body slamming into yours.


00:42:10.603 --> 00:42:11.710
Do you understand that?


00:42:11.740 --> 00:42:15.177
Pardon, sir?
What did you say?


00:42:15.178 --> 00:42:16.781
Tackle you, King.


00:42:16.811 --> 00:42:18.415
It's our only option.


00:42:26.388 --> 00:42:27.626
I don't want to die, sir.


00:42:27.656 --> 00:42:30.262
But I don't want you
to die either, sir.


00:42:30.292 --> 00:42:33.829
Maybe not. Just move on and I'll take
care of this. Don't worry about it.


00:42:33.830 --> 00:42:36.199
None of us is going
to die, King.


00:42:36.229 --> 00:42:37.536
I can do this.


00:42:37.566 --> 00:42:40.202
But I need you to let me
do the work.


00:42:40.232 --> 00:42:41.503
Do you understand?


00:42:41.504 --> 00:42:43.873
If you move, you cost us
precious milliseconds.


00:42:43.903 --> 00:42:47.543
Let me move you.
You understand?


00:42:49.345 --> 00:42:50.747
Yes, sir.


00:42:53.515 --> 00:42:56.185
When are you going
to do this, sir?


00:43:02.492 --> 00:43:04.560
I shall give you
plenty of warning.


00:43:04.590 --> 00:43:06.128
Don't worry, Mr. King.


00:43:09.064 --> 00:43:10.599
Maybe it's not such
a good idea, sir.


00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:12.702
I mean, we could always
just cut the wire...


00:43:42.731 --> 00:43:43.966
You all right?


00:43:48.470 --> 00:43:49.905
Damn!


00:43:52.075 --> 00:43:54.179
Sorry, sir.
It's my fault. I'm sorry.


00:43:54.209 --> 00:43:58.380
All right, that's enough,
I'm alive. You're alive.


00:43:58.381 --> 00:44:00.149
This is not good.


00:44:02.718 --> 00:44:03.855
Shit.


00:44:03.885 --> 00:44:05.454
What's the diagnosis, man?


00:44:05.455 --> 00:44:08.892
Well, the good news is
you've got a clean open wound.


00:44:08.922 --> 00:44:11.594
Probably some
shrapnel tearing through.


00:44:11.624 --> 00:44:14.067
The bad news is this branch.


00:44:14.097 --> 00:44:16.868
Not much bleeding
because it's an impalement.


00:44:16.898 --> 00:44:19.669
But could have lacerated
your femoral artery.


00:44:19.699 --> 00:44:23.573
And you'd bleed
to death internally.


00:44:23.603 --> 00:44:25.641
And how do we know that?


00:44:25.671 --> 00:44:27.646
You'll know.


00:44:27.676 --> 00:44:30.146
I'll just plug this hole.


00:44:31.147 --> 00:44:32.250
Stop the bleeding.


00:44:32.280 --> 00:44:37.853
And then if I dress
this branch to stabilize it.


00:44:37.854 --> 00:44:40.207
Just do as little as
you need to, Harris.


00:44:40.237 --> 00:44:42.900
We don't have much time.
That's an order.


00:44:42.930 --> 00:44:45.593
It's good the house
is not far off, sir.


00:44:45.623 --> 00:44:47.731
Quick as you can, man.


00:44:51.600 --> 00:44:53.604
Can you walk?


00:44:53.634 --> 00:44:55.638
Yes. I can try.


00:44:55.668 --> 00:44:57.307
Come on.


00:47:00.296 --> 00:47:01.733
This is it.


00:47:01.763 --> 00:47:03.201
How are you doing, sir?


00:47:03.231 --> 00:47:05.500
Still planning on
surviving this bloody war.


00:47:05.501 --> 00:47:07.755
Are you sure this
place is safe?


00:47:07.785 --> 00:47:10.039
I'm not sure about
anything anymore,


00:47:10.069 --> 00:47:12.241
but what choice
do we have?


00:47:12.271 --> 00:47:14.709
Let's go.


00:47:32.829 --> 00:47:35.365
Come in. Quickly.
Quickly.


00:47:39.001 --> 00:47:40.335
Come on, sir.


00:47:43.338 --> 00:47:44.610
Come on.


00:47:44.640 --> 00:47:46.776
Easy, sir, easy.


00:47:55.885 --> 00:47:56.952
You quite all right,
Mr. Harris?


00:47:56.982 --> 00:47:58.123
Yes, sir, just need...


00:47:58.153 --> 00:48:00.192
Let me help.
I was a nurse.


00:48:00.222 --> 00:48:02.225
I worked at Clemenceau
Hospital before it was bombed.


00:48:02.255 --> 00:48:03.593
You...
you have a radio, yes?


00:48:03.623 --> 00:48:04.931
<i>Oui.</i>


00:48:04.961 --> 00:48:07.281
But it only hails frequencies
from the Resistance.


00:48:07.311 --> 00:48:09.631
Well, I mean, is there any
way that the Resistance


00:48:09.661 --> 00:48:11.600
can get in touch with
the allies so they can


00:48:11.630 --> 00:48:13.385
let them know our whereabouts?


00:48:13.415 --> 00:48:15.141
It is possible.
I can try.


00:48:15.171 --> 00:48:17.239
All right, Harris,
you accompany our friend


00:48:17.269 --> 00:48:18.675
and see if you
can achieve that.


00:48:25.948 --> 00:48:28.050
Because this did not
hit an artery,


00:48:28.051 --> 00:48:29.355
we can remove it.


00:48:29.385 --> 00:48:31.254
And you know this how,
from your time as a nurse?


00:48:31.284 --> 00:48:34.089
I shall get
some boiling water.


00:48:37.093 --> 00:48:38.697
Sir?


00:48:38.727 --> 00:48:40.766
Thank you.


00:48:40.796 --> 00:48:42.835
I was just doing my job.


00:48:42.865 --> 00:48:47.435
No, no, it's much more than just
doing your job saving my life.


00:48:47.465 --> 00:48:49.141
You're welcome, King.


00:48:49.171 --> 00:48:53.475
So, how's it going with
the French Resistance there?


00:48:53.505 --> 00:48:54.880
No.


00:48:54.910 --> 00:48:56.430
It's, it's
not like that.


00:48:56.460 --> 00:48:57.981
I'm sure
it's not, sir.


00:49:15.597 --> 00:49:17.466
This was a
good field dressing.


00:49:19.301 --> 00:49:21.571
I'll just leave her
to tend to your wounds, sir.


00:49:22.805 --> 00:49:24.009
What?


00:49:24.039 --> 00:49:27.547
Nothing.
He's just being an idiot.


00:49:27.577 --> 00:49:31.481
He's just a little boy who
needs the love of a woman.


00:49:31.511 --> 00:49:33.281
Yeah.


00:49:37.887 --> 00:49:39.821
F13C, come in, over.


00:49:42.624 --> 00:49:44.425
Is F13C checked in yet?


00:49:44.426 --> 00:49:46.012
Negative, sir.


00:49:46.042 --> 00:49:47.571
Raise them.


00:49:47.601 --> 00:49:49.131
Yes, sir.


00:49:53.736 --> 00:49:55.422
Okay, this is going to hurt.


00:49:55.452 --> 00:49:57.138
I wish I had
some whiskey or...


00:49:57.168 --> 00:49:58.556
I never touch the stuff.


00:49:58.586 --> 00:49:59.975
- No? Really?
- Really.


00:50:00.005 --> 00:50:02.311
Why not?


00:50:02.312 --> 00:50:03.315
It's okay. It's...


00:50:03.345 --> 00:50:04.847
it's none of my business.


00:50:06.347 --> 00:50:09.684
My father was rather
too fond of the stuff.


00:50:09.714 --> 00:50:11.453
Wasn't a great man.


00:50:15.091 --> 00:50:17.259
You're a great man.


00:50:17.289 --> 00:50:19.030
No.


00:50:19.060 --> 00:50:20.329
No, I'm just a soldier.


00:50:20.330 --> 00:50:23.066
No. You are so much
more than that.


00:50:31.506 --> 00:50:33.309
I'm sorry. I...


00:50:35.912 --> 00:50:37.946
God, that hurt.


00:50:37.976 --> 00:50:39.351
I'm sorry.


00:50:39.381 --> 00:50:41.050
I thought it was better
to take you by surprise.


00:50:41.080 --> 00:50:42.785
Well, you certainly did that.


00:50:42.815 --> 00:50:45.757
Dear God, that smarts.


00:50:45.787 --> 00:50:49.191
Okay, put pressure on there.


00:50:52.695 --> 00:50:54.196
Hold it.


00:51:04.906 --> 00:51:06.609
Thank you
for trusting me.


00:51:22.925 --> 00:51:24.926
I'll say this
for these Frenchmen:


00:51:24.956 --> 00:51:27.030
they make
a damn good wine.


00:51:28.765 --> 00:51:30.966
I'm a beer man,
myself.


00:51:30.996 --> 00:51:32.901
When in Rome.


00:51:32.931 --> 00:51:34.806
Drink up.


00:51:34.836 --> 00:51:37.472
You never know
when you...


00:51:42.412 --> 00:51:43.479
Right.


00:51:53.722 --> 00:51:56.492
Have you really never
been with a woman?


00:52:00.196 --> 00:52:03.766
Well, I mean
I've kissed 'em.


00:52:03.796 --> 00:52:04.737
Lots of them.


00:52:04.767 --> 00:52:08.088
But, no,
not all the way.


00:52:08.118 --> 00:52:11.439
You're missing out, mate.


00:52:11.469 --> 00:52:13.078
Well...


00:52:13.108 --> 00:52:15.611
To me,
it's not just about sex.


00:52:18.379 --> 00:52:23.051
The more you have of a thing,
the less special it becomes.


00:52:23.081 --> 00:52:26.190
At least to me.


00:52:26.220 --> 00:52:28.156
I've always wanted it
to be with the right woman.


00:52:28.186 --> 00:52:31.394
Mate, they're all
the right woman.


00:52:36.966 --> 00:52:38.471
Hey, to be honest
with you,


00:52:38.501 --> 00:52:41.537
my first time I was
head over heels in love.


00:52:44.906 --> 00:52:48.778
We were just kids with
no idea what we were doing.


00:52:52.714 --> 00:52:54.216
But it was real.


00:53:04.526 --> 00:53:06.596
I can't imagine what I'm going
to tell Mrs. Thomas.


00:53:10.298 --> 00:53:13.034
You are going to tell her
that her man was a hero,


00:53:13.035 --> 00:53:16.406
and we wouldn't be here
if he hadn't done what he did.


00:53:18.073 --> 00:53:20.409
And if you want,
I'll go with you.


00:53:22.477 --> 00:53:24.780
Thank you.


00:53:30.285 --> 00:53:32.187
You're a good man,
Mr. Walker.


00:53:33.988 --> 00:53:37.592
No. I'm not.


00:53:39.928 --> 00:53:41.696
But I'm trying.


00:53:45.667 --> 00:53:47.670
You have your moments.


00:53:47.700 --> 00:53:49.704
All it takes is one.


00:53:50.838 --> 00:53:52.808
One good one.


00:53:57.245 --> 00:53:59.714
You should wait
for the right woman, King.


00:54:52.734 --> 00:54:56.037
F13C, this is 7, 8,
Echo, Charlie, Papa.


00:54:56.067 --> 00:54:57.710
Come in, over.


00:54:57.740 --> 00:55:03.946
Again, F13C,
this is 78ECP.


00:55:03.976 --> 00:55:05.247
Come in, over.


00:55:06.649 --> 00:55:08.484
There... there's
no response, sir.


00:55:08.514 --> 00:55:10.819
- Keep scanning.
- Yes, sir.


00:55:20.629 --> 00:55:22.735
F13C here.


00:55:22.765 --> 00:55:24.170
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:24.200 --> 00:55:27.836
Repeat, F13C,
are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:27.866 --> 00:55:29.907
F13C here.


00:55:29.937 --> 00:55:32.273
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:32.274 --> 00:55:35.012
Repeat, F13C here.


00:55:35.042 --> 00:55:37.046
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:37.076 --> 00:55:38.847
F13C, come in.


00:55:44.320 --> 00:55:45.590
Keep searching.


00:55:45.620 --> 00:55:47.656
He may be using
a different frequency.


00:55:50.892 --> 00:55:52.963
<i>F13C here.</i>


00:55:52.993 --> 00:55:54.829
<i>Are you there, Dunkirk?</i>


00:55:54.830 --> 00:55:56.201
We have a signal, sir.


00:55:56.231 --> 00:55:58.835
<i>F13C here.
Are you there, Dunkirk?</i>


00:55:58.865 --> 00:56:01.469
F13C.
This is Colonel Plummer.


00:56:01.470 --> 00:56:03.842
<i>What is your sitrep?</i>


00:56:03.872 --> 00:56:06.045
Repeat, what is your sitrep?


00:56:06.075 --> 00:56:10.212
We're at a safe house,
outside the drop coordinates,


00:56:10.242 --> 00:56:13.131
approximately
four miles northwest.


00:56:13.161 --> 00:56:16.051
Good to hear
your voices, boys.


00:56:16.081 --> 00:56:17.188
What's your situation?


00:56:17.218 --> 00:56:19.554
<i>We've lost Sgt. Thomas.</i>


00:56:19.555 --> 00:56:21.525
<i>Lieutenant Calloway
is injured,</i>


00:56:21.555 --> 00:56:23.496
but we have
secured the package.


00:56:23.526 --> 00:56:25.665
<i>We're being pursued
by Jerrys, sir.</i>


00:56:25.695 --> 00:56:28.132
<i>We're possibly going
to need air support.</i>


00:56:28.162 --> 00:56:31.733
French Resistance have had
a change of plans, so we...


00:56:31.763 --> 00:56:33.669
we may have
been compromised.


00:56:34.903 --> 00:56:36.775
Where are you heading?


00:56:36.805 --> 00:56:41.344
<i>We're heading to an airfield
about two miles from the bridge.</i>


00:56:41.374 --> 00:56:43.681
<i>The package will be
flown to mainland.</i>


00:56:43.711 --> 00:56:45.516
<i>Sir, we're going
to have to pass through</i>


00:56:45.546 --> 00:56:48.282
<i>German-occupied area
to get to the airfield.</i>


00:56:48.283 --> 00:56:49.721
<i>We may need support.</i>


00:56:49.751 --> 00:56:53.607
I'll do my best
to provide some air support.


00:56:53.637 --> 00:56:57.493
Pop some smoke so
we know where you are.


00:56:57.523 --> 00:56:58.496
<i>One more thing.</i>


00:56:58.526 --> 00:57:00.065
What's that, Colonel?


00:57:00.095 --> 00:57:03.703
There should be a bridge a few
kilometers down the main route.


00:57:03.733 --> 00:57:07.970
<i>We have reason to believe there's a
German patrol operating in that area.</i>


00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:12.041
<i>That would put a group of French
freedom fighters in danger.</i>


00:57:12.071 --> 00:57:16.410
I want you boys
to blow that bridge.


00:57:16.440 --> 00:57:17.882
But with what, sir?


00:57:17.912 --> 00:57:21.516
Walker should have
the explosives you boys need.


00:57:21.517 --> 00:57:24.287
Roger that. Out.


00:57:29.591 --> 00:57:32.560
Tell headquarters we should
send men to the bridge


00:57:32.590 --> 00:57:35.097
and to the airstrip.


00:57:47.108 --> 00:57:48.877
We have more company.


00:58:03.291 --> 00:58:04.693
Quietly.


00:58:12.033 --> 00:58:13.237
That's gotta sting.


00:58:13.267 --> 00:58:14.620
Mr. Keller, do you drink?


00:58:14.650 --> 00:58:16.004
As much as I can, ma'am.


00:58:22.044 --> 00:58:24.946
This looks like
it's going to be fine.


00:58:24.976 --> 00:58:26.083
I'll live.


00:58:26.113 --> 00:58:27.416
We'll all will.


00:58:48.303 --> 00:58:50.857
Do you see any more?


00:58:50.887 --> 00:58:53.441
Let's hide the bodies.


00:58:58.314 --> 00:59:00.049
<i>Nein.</i>


00:59:14.028 --> 00:59:16.097
<i>Ja wohl.</i>


00:59:26.106 --> 00:59:27.275
You talked to the Colonel?


00:59:27.276 --> 00:59:29.614
- Yes.
- What does he say?


00:59:29.644 --> 00:59:31.280
I managed to give him
our coordinates and then...


00:59:31.310 --> 00:59:32.451
We're out of time, sir.


00:59:32.481 --> 00:59:34.186
Why?
What's... what's happening?


00:59:34.216 --> 00:59:36.785
We just killed two Nazis who were
about to call in our position.


00:59:36.815 --> 00:59:38.757
- Damn it.
- Can you walk?


00:59:38.787 --> 00:59:40.388
Doesn't look like
I have much choice, does it?


00:59:40.418 --> 00:59:42.607
Come on, sir.
Come on.


00:59:42.637 --> 00:59:44.826
That's it.
All right.


00:59:44.827 --> 00:59:46.729
<i>Merci.</i>


01:00:01.042 --> 01:00:04.211
The airfield is
15 kilometers north.


01:00:04.241 --> 01:00:05.250
<i>Merci.</i>


01:00:05.280 --> 01:00:06.518
<i>Merci beaucoup.</i>


01:00:06.548 --> 01:00:08.654
So, yeah, thank you
for what you are doing.


01:00:08.684 --> 01:00:11.252
The Nazis are coming. You cannot
stay here, you know that.


01:00:11.282 --> 01:00:12.556
I know.


01:00:12.586 --> 01:00:14.956
I'm going to try
and buy you some more time.


01:00:16.124 --> 01:00:17.593
<i>Merci.</i>


01:00:18.993 --> 01:00:20.829
Sir, are you sure you don't
want any of that morphine?


01:00:20.859 --> 01:00:23.064
No, thank you, Harris.
It dulls the senses.


01:00:23.094 --> 01:00:25.300
Yeah, but so does having
a tree in your leg.


01:01:19.187 --> 01:01:20.891
<i>Bonjour.</i>


01:01:20.921 --> 01:01:22.625
No, no, no.


01:01:31.934 --> 01:01:35.137
It's a rather nice day
for a stroll, isn't it?


01:01:38.205 --> 01:01:41.709
And where is our French
little mouse strolling to?


01:01:47.548 --> 01:01:50.818
We can make this so much simpler
if you just tell me where she is.


01:01:52.620 --> 01:01:53.590
Who?


01:01:53.620 --> 01:01:55.791
What girl?


01:01:58.258 --> 01:02:00.162
Bring him.


01:02:00.192 --> 01:02:02.197
No, no.


01:02:02.227 --> 01:02:04.233
Wait. Wait.


01:02:07.669 --> 01:02:10.705
I don't under...
What is going...


01:03:23.512 --> 01:03:26.749
I love the smell
of burning flesh.


01:03:29.684 --> 01:03:34.326
It reminds me of how,
as a little boy,


01:03:34.356 --> 01:03:39.093
<i>my father would roast
a schwein on an open fire.</i>


01:03:47.769 --> 01:03:50.272
Now, tell me where they are.


01:03:54.575 --> 01:03:57.945
I don't know what
you're talking about.


01:04:20.328 --> 01:04:23.197
Now tell me everything
or you will die.


01:04:24.132 --> 01:04:27.535
Okay, okay.


01:04:30.838 --> 01:04:32.974
Everything, I'll tell you.


01:04:36.043 --> 01:04:39.084
They are...


01:04:39.114 --> 01:04:41.250
heading into the village.


01:04:47.188 --> 01:04:52.027
Now, why would they
be going into a village


01:04:52.057 --> 01:04:55.230
that is crawling
with Germans?


01:04:57.931 --> 01:05:00.971
Ex... exactly.


01:05:01.001 --> 01:05:04.405
That is the last place you
would expect to see them.


01:05:07.175 --> 01:05:11.780
Do I look,
stupid to you?


01:05:11.810 --> 01:05:13.648
Honest answer?


01:05:17.918 --> 01:05:19.187
<i>Oui.</i>


01:05:23.491 --> 01:05:25.427
So be it.


01:05:29.797 --> 01:05:33.901
For your information,
I know that the girl


01:05:33.902 --> 01:05:39.441
is trying to escape by plane
from a small airfield.


01:05:42.943 --> 01:05:45.146
Not so stupid now, am I?


01:06:36.533 --> 01:06:38.336
Do you need to stop?


01:06:40.870 --> 01:06:42.506
Perhaps just
for a moment.


01:06:50.113 --> 01:06:53.353
By my calculations,
we are here,


01:06:53.383 --> 01:06:56.186
so it should be just
beyond this next ridge.


01:06:56.216 --> 01:06:57.921
You're never gonna
make it on that leg.


01:06:57.951 --> 01:06:59.522
That's at least
another six miles.


01:06:59.552 --> 01:07:00.627
I'll manage.


01:07:00.657 --> 01:07:02.894
You may not have to.


01:07:05.528 --> 01:07:07.097
What do you mean?


01:07:09.300 --> 01:07:10.802
Well, shit.


01:07:10.832 --> 01:07:12.335
Take cover.


01:07:32.122 --> 01:07:34.023
You know, I could probably
just pick him off


01:07:34.024 --> 01:07:36.426
from about a hundred
yards with this rifle.


01:07:36.456 --> 01:07:38.628
You snipers are
all the same.


01:07:38.629 --> 01:07:42.633
Trust me, mate, these blokes
will piss their pants.


01:07:42.663 --> 01:07:44.702
Yes, well, we'll see
about that, won't we?


01:08:07.289 --> 01:08:09.159
Be ready,
here they come.


01:08:25.108 --> 01:08:28.980
Help! Help!


01:08:30.213 --> 01:08:32.314
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot.


01:08:32.315 --> 01:08:34.018
Please, no, don't shoot.


01:08:34.048 --> 01:08:35.751
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot.


01:08:35.752 --> 01:08:37.488
Don't shoot me.
Please, no, don't shoot.


01:08:37.518 --> 01:08:39.522
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot, please.


01:08:39.552 --> 01:08:41.492
Hello, mates.


01:08:48.164 --> 01:08:50.368
Good afternoon, gentlemen.


01:08:54.538 --> 01:08:56.075
I can't believe
that worked.


01:08:56.105 --> 01:08:57.940
What would you do
if a big bald bastard


01:08:57.970 --> 01:09:00.043
tossed a grenade
in your vehicle?


01:09:00.073 --> 01:09:01.511
Fair point.


01:09:35.078 --> 01:09:36.597
It's quiet.
I don't like it.


01:09:36.627 --> 01:09:38.117
This should do the trick.


01:09:38.147 --> 01:09:39.516
Once we destroy it,
that should slow them down.


01:09:39.546 --> 01:09:40.783
- Mr. Harris?
- Sir?


01:09:40.813 --> 01:09:42.051
You stay and look out.


01:09:42.052 --> 01:09:44.187
Mr. King, Mr. Walker, would
you kindly assist me in rigging?


01:09:44.217 --> 01:09:45.955
The pleasure would
be mine, sir.


01:09:45.985 --> 01:09:47.361
Come along, King.


01:09:47.391 --> 01:09:49.827
You seem to like
explosives today.


01:10:59.195 --> 01:11:00.829
How are we doing, gentlemen?


01:11:00.859 --> 01:11:02.882
Getting there, sir.


01:11:02.912 --> 01:11:04.905
Sergeant Walker?


01:11:04.935 --> 01:11:06.602
A few more moments, please.


01:11:06.632 --> 01:11:07.704
Very well.


01:11:11.541 --> 01:11:13.709
How's it going
down there, chaps?


01:11:13.739 --> 01:11:15.028
Almost done.


01:11:15.058 --> 01:11:16.347
Make it quick.


01:11:19.583 --> 01:11:23.057
Is this the bridge?
Here?


01:11:23.087 --> 01:11:24.958
The open space on the other
side of this tree line


01:11:24.988 --> 01:11:28.191
has a hangar-like structure.
It's got to be the way out.


01:11:29.626 --> 01:11:31.429
Sir, if I'm reading
this map correctly,


01:11:31.459 --> 01:11:33.262
then the airfield
should just be on


01:11:33.292 --> 01:11:34.735
the other side of this forest.


01:11:34.765 --> 01:11:36.699
- Where's Walker and King?
- Just finishing up.


01:11:36.729 --> 01:11:38.135
They should be up
momentarily.


01:11:38.165 --> 01:11:39.436
I hope so.


01:11:43.006 --> 01:11:43.977
Do you hear that?


01:11:44.007 --> 01:11:45.379
That doesn't sound good.


01:11:45.409 --> 01:11:47.311
Doesn't sound like
a lot of fun.


01:11:47.341 --> 01:11:48.912
Mr. Walker?


01:11:48.913 --> 01:11:50.147
How are we
doing down there?


01:11:50.177 --> 01:11:51.584
Almost there, sir.


01:11:51.614 --> 01:11:54.385
Well, hurry up!
We have to go!


01:12:03.327 --> 01:12:05.529
- Start the car.
- It won't start, sir.


01:12:05.559 --> 01:12:06.932
Quick as you can, man.


01:12:06.962 --> 01:12:08.631
It won't start, sir.
It won't start.


01:12:08.632 --> 01:12:10.768
- Let's go!
- It won't start.


01:12:31.521 --> 01:12:34.890
Drop your weapons
and surrender.


01:12:34.891 --> 01:12:37.498
You have nowhere to go.


01:12:37.528 --> 01:12:41.049
It's a bloody tank.
Damn it.


01:12:41.079 --> 01:12:44.601
This is your final warning.


01:12:46.569 --> 01:12:49.271
Drop your weapons
and surrender.


01:12:49.301 --> 01:12:51.941
Damn, it's a ruddy tank!


01:12:54.177 --> 01:12:56.145
- We'll have to go on foot!
- Let's go!


01:12:58.181 --> 01:12:59.483
Go, go, go!


01:13:01.217 --> 01:13:04.120
Fire!


01:14:04.780 --> 01:14:07.984
Did you really think that
you could escape from me?


01:14:08.014 --> 01:14:10.821
We monitored
your radio transmissions.


01:15:27.965 --> 01:15:29.401
Are we good?


01:15:29.431 --> 01:15:30.868
We're good.


01:15:43.012 --> 01:15:45.614
I do not understand
how anyone could like


01:15:45.644 --> 01:15:47.784
such an inferior race.


01:15:49.520 --> 01:15:52.190
They're all like rats.


01:15:52.220 --> 01:15:54.861
Don't you know this?


01:15:54.891 --> 01:15:58.261
All they have
ever done was lie,


01:15:58.291 --> 01:16:01.031
steal, and cheat.


01:16:02.565 --> 01:16:04.635
And you support them?


01:16:06.435 --> 01:16:11.807
Now, we could have easily
slaughtered you Brits at Dunkirk.


01:16:11.837 --> 01:16:14.843
But we offered you
a second chance,


01:16:14.873 --> 01:16:17.817
a chance to align with us.


01:16:17.847 --> 01:16:22.151
Let's just see if your
Mr. Winston Churchill


01:16:22.181 --> 01:16:24.223
makes the right decision.


01:16:24.253 --> 01:16:27.441
If it were up to me,
I would have killed


01:16:27.471 --> 01:16:30.660
every last one
of you on that beach.


01:16:31.961 --> 01:16:34.998
But you will all
die here today.


01:16:36.365 --> 01:16:38.135
Do you realize this?


01:16:42.437 --> 01:16:44.173
And I will decide how.


01:16:48.677 --> 01:16:52.414
And as for you, French,


01:16:52.444 --> 01:16:54.984
you disgust me!


01:17:07.597 --> 01:17:10.851
Now personally, I would love


01:17:10.881 --> 01:17:14.136
to kill you
right here and now.


01:17:18.408 --> 01:17:21.313
But apparently...


01:17:21.343 --> 01:17:27.216
You have some information in that
French little brain of yours.


01:17:32.721 --> 01:17:37.293
That is very valuable
to us.


01:17:45.101 --> 01:17:48.972
Now, I will ask you
one simple question


01:17:50.873 --> 01:17:53.609
and you will answer me.


01:17:55.377 --> 01:17:57.647
What is the algorithm?


01:18:17.734 --> 01:18:22.873
What is the algorithm!?


01:18:24.440 --> 01:18:26.042
Bitch.


01:18:30.547 --> 01:18:32.384
I will count down from five,


01:18:32.414 --> 01:18:34.283
and then you will tell me
the algorithm.


01:18:36.720 --> 01:18:38.387
Okay. I will tell you!
I will tell you.


01:18:38.417 --> 01:18:39.655
Don't tell him anything!


01:18:43.927 --> 01:18:44.962
<i>Zwei.</i>


01:18:46.930 --> 01:18:47.897
<i>Eins.</i>


01:19:59.235 --> 01:20:01.337
You go on ahead.
I'll catch you up.


01:20:01.367 --> 01:20:02.538
Let me help you, sir.


01:20:09.445 --> 01:20:10.980
Fire!


01:20:13.583 --> 01:20:15.352
Cover and fire!


01:20:32.903 --> 01:20:34.870
Take cover!


01:20:58.761 --> 01:21:00.199
You all right, Mr. King?


01:21:00.229 --> 01:21:02.298
Yes, sir, just a nick.
I'm fine.


01:21:04.699 --> 01:21:06.736
All right.
Stay low. Stay low.


01:21:08.870 --> 01:21:10.873
We need to slow them down.


01:21:34.931 --> 01:21:36.832
You have nowhere to go!


01:21:36.862 --> 01:21:38.769
Surrender!


01:21:40.369 --> 01:21:42.805
More tension.
More tension.


01:21:44.539 --> 01:21:49.311
Surrender and give us the girl
and you will all go free.


01:21:53.882 --> 01:21:56.103
You will not escape.


01:21:56.133 --> 01:21:58.324
You will not get away.


01:21:58.354 --> 01:22:01.057
No one's going
to surrender, Fritz.


01:22:08.064 --> 01:22:09.499
How we doing, lads?


01:22:09.529 --> 01:22:11.534
One minute.


01:22:23.846 --> 01:22:25.985
Surrender!


01:22:26.015 --> 01:22:28.118
Okay, we're so close.


01:22:29.319 --> 01:22:30.255
Ready, sir.


01:22:30.285 --> 01:22:32.057
You will not
get out of there.


01:22:32.087 --> 01:22:34.423
Lay down covering fire
and move on my three,


01:22:34.453 --> 01:22:36.825
two, one... fire!


01:22:42.966 --> 01:22:44.151
Shit.


01:22:44.181 --> 01:22:45.367
Move!


01:22:46.970 --> 01:22:48.571
Move! Move!


01:22:49.672 --> 01:22:51.474
Go, go, go.


01:24:27.602 --> 01:24:29.541
For King and country.


01:24:29.571 --> 01:24:31.541
I'm willing to bet
Fritz is still coming.


01:24:31.571 --> 01:24:33.142
So let's go.


01:24:40.917 --> 01:24:42.254
Where is the plane?


01:24:42.284 --> 01:24:43.586
It's supposed to be here.


01:24:52.528 --> 01:24:54.129
No!


01:25:13.682 --> 01:25:15.284
You have nowhere to go!


01:25:21.157 --> 01:25:23.196
Surrender.


01:25:23.226 --> 01:25:26.996
Brother by my side,
what do you want to do?


01:25:27.026 --> 01:25:28.897
I have one magazine left.


01:25:28.927 --> 01:25:30.602
No. No.


01:25:30.632 --> 01:25:32.767
Drop your weapons.


01:25:32.797 --> 01:25:34.503
Do it now!


01:25:39.342 --> 01:25:42.045
You are totally surrounded.


01:25:44.779 --> 01:25:46.515
Bloody hell, I'm not
going out like this.


01:25:46.516 --> 01:25:48.718
- No!
- Stand down, Sergeant Walker.


01:25:48.748 --> 01:25:50.519
It's our only chance.


01:25:54.989 --> 01:25:56.960
I'm sorry, Angelique.


01:25:56.990 --> 01:25:58.660
We did all we could.


01:25:58.690 --> 01:26:00.145
Please, no.
Please, no.


01:26:00.175 --> 01:26:01.601
Please don't give up hope.


01:26:01.631 --> 01:26:04.367
It wasn't supposed
to end like this.


01:26:06.401 --> 01:26:07.703
Fire.


01:26:09.004 --> 01:26:11.106
Look. Look!


01:26:17.113 --> 01:26:18.785
It's our boys.


01:26:18.815 --> 01:26:20.717
It's about bloody time.


01:27:05.962 --> 01:27:07.530
<i>Schiesse.</i>


01:27:09.030 --> 01:27:10.833
<i>Schiesse.</i>


01:28:05.120 --> 01:28:08.856
See, you never
give up hope.


01:28:08.886 --> 01:28:10.396
We did it.


01:28:10.426 --> 01:28:13.631
God save the King.


01:28:13.661 --> 01:28:16.866
We did it.
We did it!


01:28:25.574 --> 01:28:26.879
Let's get her to that plane.


01:28:26.909 --> 01:28:29.679
You took the words
right out of my mouth.


01:29:15.056 --> 01:29:16.693
Thank you.


01:29:18.159 --> 01:29:19.695
Thank you.


01:29:21.596 --> 01:29:23.131
I'm sorry for your men.


01:29:23.132 --> 01:29:25.538
But thank you for my life.


01:29:25.568 --> 01:29:28.271
I just hope it
was worth it, love.


01:29:28.301 --> 01:29:30.439
It is.


01:29:35.444 --> 01:29:37.115
Could you do us a favor?


01:29:37.145 --> 01:29:40.581
When you get back to London,
find Emily Thomas.


01:29:40.582 --> 01:29:42.687
Give her this letter.


01:29:42.717 --> 01:29:44.820
I don't think I'll be around
to give it to her.


01:29:44.850 --> 01:29:46.954
And I'd rather she got it
sooner than later.


01:29:46.984 --> 01:29:48.456
Of course.


01:29:48.486 --> 01:29:49.958
Thank you.


01:29:54.663 --> 01:29:57.499
Let's get you on that plane.


01:29:57.529 --> 01:29:59.502
Are you all right?


01:29:59.532 --> 01:30:01.240
You?


01:30:01.270 --> 01:30:03.342
I'm alive.


01:30:03.372 --> 01:30:05.559
I don't know how,
but I am.


01:30:05.589 --> 01:30:07.746
You must never
give up hope.


01:30:07.776 --> 01:30:10.863
It doesn't matter how,
it matters why.


01:30:10.893 --> 01:30:13.981
You are a special man,
Lieutenant.


01:30:14.011 --> 01:30:15.916
You have a purpose.


01:30:15.946 --> 01:30:17.852
You must trust that.


01:30:17.882 --> 01:30:19.592
Thank you.


01:30:19.622 --> 01:30:22.527
Those men died heroes.


01:30:22.557 --> 01:30:24.694
Is there a better way
to serve your country?


01:30:24.724 --> 01:30:26.264
None.


01:30:26.294 --> 01:30:28.115
What will you do now?


01:30:28.145 --> 01:30:29.966
Will I see you again?


01:30:32.235 --> 01:30:34.272
This war is
far from over.


01:30:34.302 --> 01:30:39.240
I'll just have to enjoy the
beauty this world has to offer.


01:30:39.270 --> 01:30:42.912
When one remembers to
look beyond the ugliness.


01:30:59.294 --> 01:31:01.032
I'll see you in London.


01:31:01.062 --> 01:31:03.833
Now, let's get you
on that plane.


01:31:53.815 --> 01:31:55.583
I think she
likes you, sir.


01:31:55.613 --> 01:31:57.885
I don't know.


01:31:57.886 --> 01:32:00.323
Did you see the way
she looked at me just now?


01:32:00.353 --> 01:32:02.291
There might be
a real future there.


01:32:05.321 --> 01:32:23.321
<font color=#ff0000>subs4free.info</font>

